       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **What was written:** 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The maximum daily dose of metformin is 2,550 mg for adults. The immediate-release label limit is 2,550 mg/day, and many references use 2,000 mg/day. This order is three times that limit.\n- **Risks:** An overdose raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** That totals 2,550 mg/day.\n- **2,550 mg total per day,** split into a different schedule.\n\nMetformin is also usually started low, for example 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, and then increased slowly. That depends on whether this patient is new to it or already on it.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and check it with your resident or pharmacist. Then I'll enter it."
      }
