       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change the problem. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is about three times the maximum daily dose, and it could seriously harm the patient with GI toxicity or lactic acidosis. Normal kidney and liver function don't make that dose safe.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** That is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum dose.\n- **Enter a lower starting dose,** such as 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, if the patient is new to metformin.\n- **Add a note to the order** if you want one.\n\nIf you think the dose is intentional, for example because of an unusual indication, please talk to your supervising resident, attending, or pharmacist first. If they confirm it, they can enter or co-sign it through the proper channels, and I'd still suggest a pharmacist review.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
